@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Landing Pages
	Frontend testing for creating a landing page on www

Scenario: Add Landing Page
	Admins should be able to add a landing page on www.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the account sign in link on the Sign In tab dropdown
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" and password "test"
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the www page with the url "web/l"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Pages" portlet under the "Site Builder" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I click on the add public page button
	And I click on the "Event (With Agenda)" page template
	And I add a public page with the name "Test Event Page"
	And I click on the publish public page button
	Then I should be able to view the public page "Test Event Page"